10. MOTION DESIGN: ABSOLUTELY CRITICAL
======================================

The animation quality is one of the most important requirements.

I want buttery-smooth, soft, natural motion.

The website must NOT feel robotic.

Use motion that feels organic and intentional.

PREFERRED MOTION:

* Gentle floating.
* Slow drifting.
* Soft easing.
* Natural acceleration and deceleration.
* Subtle rotations.
* Light spring effects.
* Small character reactions.
* Smooth opacity transitions.
* Soft scale transitions.
* Delicate parallax.
* Carefully timed cinematic scene transitions.

Use easing curves similar to:
cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)

Use spring animations only where they feel appropriate.

Do not apply the same bounce animation to every element.

Each scene should have its own motion personality:

* Gift scene: anticipation and playful interaction.
* Rocket scene: acceleration, flight, and cinematic impact.
* Memory scene: gentle, intimate transitions.
* Studio scene: playful character movement.
* Finale: floating, dreamy, emotional motion.

PERFORMANCE:

* Prefer transform and opacity animations.
* Avoid expensive layout recalculations.
* Avoid animating large blur filters continuously.
* Avoid excessive particle counts.
* Avoid unnecessary canvas rendering.
* Avoid animations that cause horizontal scrolling.
* Aim for smooth 60 FPS performance on ordinary laptops and modern phones.

ACCESSIBILITY:

* Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
* Provide visible keyboard focus.
* Ensure interactive elements can be reached with a keyboard.
* Make text readable against its background.
* Do not rely on animation alone to communicate important information.

